<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  DeepDesertTribes.xml                    Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-14
  ============================================================================

  Builds FACTION_SPEC.md section 4, "Deep Desert Tribes ; PATCH vanilla
  `TribeCivil`". A reskin, not a new def, plus the ONE group maker the spec
  explicitly orders added.

  READ FROM THE SHIPPED DEF, 2026-08-14 ; not inferred:
  C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\RimWorld\Data\Core\Defs\
    FactionDefs\Factions_Misc.xml

      ParentName                  TribeBase
      OWN nodes                   defName · label · description · colorSpectrum ·
                                  disallowedMemes · maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation ·
                                  configurationListOrderPriority
      label                       gentle tribe

  🔴 EVERYTHING ELSE IS ON THE ABSTRACT PARENT, NOT ON THIS DEF.
  `TribeBase` carries `pawnSingular`, `pawnsPlural`, `leaderTitle`,
  `settlementGenerationWeight` and all twelve `pawnGroupMakers`.
  PatchOperations run BEFORE def inheritance is resolved, so `TribeCivil` has
  none of those nodes at patch time and a `Replace` on any of them matches ZERO
  and logs red. They are `Add`s onto the child. The child's own node wins at
  inheritance, so the override reaches `TribeCivil` ALONE ; patching `TribeBase`
  would also hit TribeRough, TribeSavage and every modded descendant.

      pawnSingular / pawnsPlural  parent      ->  Add
      leaderTitle                 parent      ->  Add
      settlementGenerationWeight  parent (1)  ->  Add
      label / description         own nodes   ->  Replace
      permanentEnemy              ABSENT in the whole chain, so already false

  ⚠️ The spec's `permanentEnemy false` is the vessel's default and the reskin
  contract writes that field "only where it differs from the vessel's default".
  `TribeBase` and `TribeCivil` both omit it, and `TribeSavageBase` is a
  DIFFERENT parent. So nothing is written; the field is already false.

  ⛔ `factionNameMaker` and the raid curves are untouched.

  THE WATER RAID  (the one sanctioned group addition)
  ==================================================
  🔴 SUPERSEDED by AUTHORED_KINDS_MUST_FIELD_1 below, 2026-08-22. This section
  describes the file's original 2026-08-14 shape (ONE added group, vanilla
  `Tribal_*` kinds throughout, `pawnGroupMakers` appended rather than
  declared). That shape shipped bare-handed raiders and was replaced outright
  ; the mechanism notes on `li`-list append vs `Inherit="False"` below are
  still accurate and still the reason the fix needed `Inherit="False"`, but
  the water raid's actual, current composition, kind count and MayRequire
  status are stated only in AUTHORED_KINDS_MUST_FIELD_1's block, not here.

  Vanilla lists twelve group makers on `TribeBase` and the child inherits them.
  RimWorld's inheritance MERGES `li` lists: the child's items are APPENDED to
  the parent's unless the node carries `Inherit="False"`. Verified against
  vanilla's own defs, e.g. `HoldingPlatform` adds one `<comps>` li to
  `HoldingPlatformBase`'s three and ends up with four, while
  `Horaxian_Gunner` has to write `Inherit="False"` on `weaponTags` precisely
  because appending is the default.

  ⚠️ "Targets containers, disengages once loaded" is a RAID STRATEGY and an
  arrival mode, and a `pawnGroupMaker` expresses NEITHER. What a group maker
  can express is composition and size, so the signature is carried by those:
  `maxTotalPoints` 800 caps it to a light party (vanilla precedent, the
  Drifter group at 1000). No `Tribal_HeavyArcher`/`Jawa_DeepDesert_Heavy`, no
  `Tribal_Breacher`, no chiefs ; a breacher is the exact opposite of a group
  that leaves once it has the water. Commonality 30 against the parent's
  100/60/60/5 (superseded numbers below — the four combat groups are no
  longer the parent's).

  SAFETY
  ======
  Everything sits inside a conditional on the def existing, so the file is a
  silent no-op rather than a wall of red if the vessel ever moves.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- "gentle tribe" -> the campaign name. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>Deep Desert Tribes</label></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]/description</xpath>
          <value>
            <description>Territorial clans of the deep sand and the canyon country, for whom water is sacred and moisture farming is sacrilege — a theft from the world, committed in the open, every hour of every day.\n\nThey arrive fast, hit hard, and are gone.</description>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- Inherited from TribeBase. Add, not Replace. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><pawnSingular>Tusken raider</pawnSingular></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><pawnsPlural>Tusken raiders</pawnsPlural></value>
        </li>

        <!-- "chief" on the parent -> War Chief. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><leaderTitle>War Chief</leaderTitle></value>
        </li>

        <!-- 1 on the parent -> 1.3. Nine settlements, deep desert and canyons. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><settlementGenerationWeight>1.3</settlementGenerationWeight></value>
        </li>

        <!--
          ================================================================
          🔴 THE GROUPS ARE NOW DECLARED OUTRIGHT, NOT APPENDED.
          AUTHORED_KINDS_MUST_FIELD_1, 2026-08-22
          ================================================================
          This op used to add ONE group - the water raid - and its comment said
          "Appended to TribeBase's twelve, not replacing them." That was accurate
          and it was the bug: all four `Jawa_DeepDesert_*` kinds existed, this file
          contained the string `Jawa_DeepDesert` ZERO times, and TribeCivil fielded
          vanilla tribals exclusively. Measured live: 18 spawns from TribeCivil drew
          nerve spikers, thrumbungus shrooms and throwing knives, and 6 of 18 arrived
          bare-handed. DECIDE ruled every authored kind must be FIELDED
          (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/pawnkind_roster.md).

          🔑 WHY `Inherit="False"` HERE AND SIX `Replace`s IN BlackstarCompany.xml.
          DECIDE's ruling names the shape as "rewrite the options inside the COMBAT
          groups". That shape is REACHABLE ON `Pirate`, which writes its own six
          groups, and NOT REACHABLE HERE: `TribeCivil` inherits all twelve from the
          abstract `TribeBase`, PatchOperations run BEFORE inheritance resolves, and
          a Replace on the child therefore matches ZERO and logs nothing. Verified
          with lxml against the shipped Core XML, 2026-08-22:
              /Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]/pawnGroupMakers  ->  0 nodes
          ⛔ Patching `TribeBase` by @Name instead would hit TribeRough, TribeSavage
          and every modded descendant in 578 mods. That is not an option.

          ⇒ The only route to "zero vanilla kinds in a combat group" is to declare
          the whole list on the child and stop inheriting. DECIDE's ⛔ against
          `Inherit="False"` was that it DROPS Trader, Peaceful and Settlement, and
          the 48-kind roster has no trader role to replace them with. That objection
          is answered by RE-DECLARING those eight groups here, byte-for-byte from
          `TribeBase`, rather than by leaving them out.
          🔑 The eight non-combat groups below were COPIED PROGRAMMATICALLY out of
          Core's Factions_Misc.xml, not retyped, and they keep their vanilla
          `Tribal_*` kinds on purpose - DECIDE: "Non-combat groups stay vanilla."
          ⚠️ The cost, stated plainly: TribeCivil no longer picks up anything a
          future vanilla patch or another mod adds to TribeBase's group list. On a
          world that is hand-made once and frozen, that is a price worth paying;
          on a living mod list it would not be.

          The four combat groups keep vanilla's own commonality and each group's
          tactical character - mixed, ranged, melee, breacher - with the Tusken
          roster in place of the tribals. The water raid is the fifth, unchanged in
          shape (commonality 30, maxTotalPoints 800) but now carrying the two FAST,
          LIGHT authored kinds instead of three vanilla ones. No Heavy in it: a
          brute is the opposite of a party that leaves once it has the water.
        -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <pawnGroupMakers Inherit="False">
              <li>
                <kindDef>Combat</kindDef>
                <commonality>100</commonality>
                <options>
                    <Jawa_DeepDesert_Grunt>10</Jawa_DeepDesert_Grunt>
                    <Jawa_DeepDesert_Heavy>5</Jawa_DeepDesert_Heavy>
                    <Jawa_DeepDesert_Specialist>6</Jawa_DeepDesert_Specialist>
                </options>
              </li>
              <li>
                <kindDef>Combat</kindDef>
                <commonality>60</commonality>
                <options>
                    <Jawa_DeepDesert_Specialist>10</Jawa_DeepDesert_Specialist>
                    <Jawa_DeepDesert_Grunt>4</Jawa_DeepDesert_Grunt>
                </options>
              </li>
              <li>
                <kindDef>Combat</kindDef>
                <commonality>60</commonality>
                <options>
                    <Jawa_DeepDesert_Grunt>10</Jawa_DeepDesert_Grunt>
                    <Jawa_DeepDesert_Heavy>8</Jawa_DeepDesert_Heavy>
                </options>
              </li>
              <li>
                <kindDef>Combat</kindDef>
                <commonality>5</commonality>
                <options>
                    <Jawa_DeepDesert_Heavy>10</Jawa_DeepDesert_Heavy>
                    <Jawa_DeepDesert_Grunt>5</Jawa_DeepDesert_Grunt>
                </options>
              </li>
              <li>
                      <!-- Peaceful -->
                      <kindDef>Peaceful</kindDef>
                      <options>
                        <Tribal_Warrior>20</Tribal_Warrior>
                        <Tribal_Child MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">10</Tribal_Child>
                        <Tribal_Archer>10</Tribal_Archer>
                        <Tribal_Hunter>10</Tribal_Hunter>
                        <Tribal_HeavyArcher>10</Tribal_HeavyArcher>
                        <Tribal_Berserker>5</Tribal_Berserker>
                        <Tribal_ChiefRanged>3</Tribal_ChiefRanged>
                        <Tribal_ChiefMelee>1.5</Tribal_ChiefMelee>
                      </options>
                    </li>
              <li>
                      <kindDef>Trader</kindDef>
                      <traders>
                        <Tribal_Trader>1</Tribal_Trader>
                      </traders>
                      <carriers>
                        <Muffalo>6</Muffalo>
                        <Dromedary>5</Dromedary>
                        <Alpaca>2.5</Alpaca>
                        <Elephant>2</Elephant>
                      </carriers>
                      <guards>
                        <Tribal_Warrior>7</Tribal_Warrior>
                        <Tribal_Archer>10</Tribal_Archer>
                        <Tribal_Hunter>10</Tribal_Hunter>
                        <Tribal_HeavyArcher>10</Tribal_HeavyArcher>
                        <Tribal_Berserker>7</Tribal_Berserker>
                      </guards>
                    </li>
              <li>
                      <kindDef>Settlement</kindDef>
                      <options>
                        <Tribal_Warrior>7</Tribal_Warrior>
                        <Tribal_Archer>10</Tribal_Archer>
                        <Tribal_Hunter>10</Tribal_Hunter>
                        <Tribal_HeavyArcher>10</Tribal_HeavyArcher>
                        <Tribal_Berserker>7</Tribal_Berserker>
                        <Tribal_ChiefRanged>10</Tribal_ChiefRanged>
                      </options>
                    </li>
              <li>
                      <kindDef>Settlement_RangedOnly</kindDef>
                      <options>
                        <Tribal_Archer>10</Tribal_Archer>
                        <Tribal_Hunter>10</Tribal_Hunter>
                        <Tribal_HeavyArcher>10</Tribal_HeavyArcher>
                        <Tribal_ChiefRanged>10</Tribal_ChiefRanged>
                      </options>
                    </li>
              <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
                      <kindDef>Miners</kindDef>
                      <commonality>1</commonality>
                      <options>
                        <Tribal_Miner>1</Tribal_Miner>
                      </options>
                    </li>
              <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
                      <kindDef>Hunters</kindDef>
                      <commonality>1</commonality>
                      <options>
                        <Tribal_Hunter>1</Tribal_Hunter>
                      </options>
                    </li>
              <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
                      <kindDef>Loggers</kindDef>
                      <commonality>1</commonality>
                      <options>
                        <Tribal_Logger>1</Tribal_Logger>
                      </options>
                    </li>
              <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
                      <kindDef>Farmers</kindDef>
                      <commonality>1</commonality>
                      <options>
                        <Tribal_Farmer>1</Tribal_Farmer>
                      </options>
                    </li>

              <!-- The water raid. FACTION_SPEC.md section 4's one sanctioned addition. -->
              <li>
                <kindDef>Combat</kindDef>
                <commonality>30</commonality>
                <maxTotalPoints>800</maxTotalPoints>
                <options>
                  <Jawa_DeepDesert_Grunt>10</Jawa_DeepDesert_Grunt>
                  <Jawa_DeepDesert_Specialist>8</Jawa_DeepDesert_Specialist>
                </options>
              </li>
            </pawnGroupMakers>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- The war chief. A leader is generated once per faction and is never rolled
             into a raid, so he belongs in `fixedLeaderKinds`, not in a group maker.
             No vanilla FactionDef in Factions_Misc.xml writes this field, so ADD. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <fixedLeaderKinds>
              <li>Jawa_DeepDesert_Leader</li>
            </fixedLeaderKinds>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!--
          ================================================================
          faction_religions_spec.md entry 4 (B54)
          ================================================================
          `ideoName` and `ideoDescription` verbatim; they are the only strings
          the engine renders. ⛔ `hiddenIdeo` MUST STAY UNSET or the
          description is never shown. Structure meme goes FIRST in
          `forcedMemes`.

          🔴 `TribeCivil` ships `disallowedMemes` = Supremacist · PainIsVirtue ·
          Nudism · Raider · Blindsight — and this faith FORCES both `Raider` and
          `PainIsVirtue`. Forcing a meme the same def disallows is a direct
          contradiction, so the node is removed rather than edited.
        -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]/disallowedMemes</xpath>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <fixedIdeo>true</fixedIdeo>
            <requiredPreceptsOnly>true</requiredPreceptsOnly>
            <ideoName>the Sun-Debt</ideoName>
            <ideoDescription>The sun lends and the sand collects. Every mouthful you drink is borrowed, and the interest is paid in walking, in thirst, and in the marks we cut to remember the walking. A machine that pulls water out of the air is a thief standing between us and what we owe — it does not steal the water, it steals the debt. We take back what was drawn. We never take more than was drawn.</ideoDescription>
            <forcedMemes>
              <li>Structure_Animist</li>
              <li>NaturePrimacy</li>
              <li>Raider</li>
              <li MayRequire="vanillaquestsexpanded.generator">VQE_Technophobia</li>
              <li>PainIsVirtue</li>
            </forcedMemes>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- Bespoke world-map icon. the def does NOT write it - it inherits Expanding/Village from TribeBase, so ADD.
             A Replace here would match nothing and log nothing. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><factionIconPath>World/JawaFactions/DeepDesertTribes</factionIconPath></value>
        </li>

        <!-- The name the world object carries. No vanilla FactionDef writes fixedName
             (checked in Core/Defs/FactionDefs/Factions_Misc.xml), so this is an ADD.
             A Replace would match nothing and log red. factionNameMaker stays: it still
             names this faction's SETTLEMENTS. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><fixedName>Deep Desert Tribes</fixedName></value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- ═══ LEADER_TITLES_ON_THE_IDEO_1, 2026-08-22 ═══════════════════════════════
       `Faction.LeaderTitle` (RimWorld/Faction.cs:142) prefers the primary IDEO's
       `leaderTitleMale` and only falls back to `def.leaderTitle`. Measured live:
       the ideo overrode the def on 36 of 37 factions, so the Deep Desert Tribes' authored
       title "War Chief" was never the word a player read. The ideo's title is
       generated from its CULTURE's `leaderTitleMaker`, so the route is a culture
       of our own - full mechanism in `Defs/CultureDefs/JawaLeaderTitles.xml`.
       ⛔ Not a patch on the shared vanilla culture: Corunan is shared with every
       faction of its category in 578 mods and patching it renames all of them.
       ⚠️ This BAKES at world creation and cannot be retrofitted. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]</xpath>
      <value><allowedCultures Inherit="False"><li>Jawa_Culture_DeepDesert</li></allowedCultures></value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
